The interviewer asks why the speaker keeps going, keeps pursuing tech, and keeps creating more companies. The important feature of the question is timing. It is not the beginner’s question about survival. It is the post-success question: $\text{exit}+\text{freedom}
\quad\Longrightarrow\quad
\text{why build again?}$ The speaker’s answer first rejects a simple hustle story. He says he did that for a while and burned out. He had worked hard while young, sold his company, and thought what he wanted next was travel.

