The post-exit sequence is concrete: $\text{intense early work}
\longrightarrow
\text{company sale}
\longrightarrow
\text{burnout}
\longrightarrow
\text{large yacht and years of travel}.$ This is anecdote, not doctrine. But it matters because the speaker did not merely imagine leisure. He tried it seriously enough for its limits to appear.

