p.src:
This addition changes the book’s resilience argument. The problem is not simply too much work. It is the fit between the builder’s energy and the structure carrying it. Too much unfiltered work can burn the founder out; too little meaningful structure can let boredom become its own danger. The durable answer in this interview is not more pressure, but better fit: $\text{sustainable next project}
=
\text{creative drive}
+
\text{genuine interest}
+
\text{chosen commitment}.$

